        "id": 103444,
        "name": "JimB",
        "username": "JimB",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jimb/{size}/2093_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-07-11T04:34:47.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Good god.</p>\n<p>Only Engine of War Bunker survived the assault on the Chairman in Silver Gulch.  No one had the ability to inflict damage across wide groups of targets, and of course they kept slamming out underbosses and thugs and bringing them back out with Prison Breaks.  At the end, the villain deck had been shuffled, and a desperate Bunker had nothing out but a Grenade Launcher, a Maintenance Unit, and a Turret Mode, and he was very lucky that each of his flipped teammates had the ability to let him use a power.  He was regaining 6 HP a round and generally losing slightly less than that from counterattacks until finally the Chairman fell down and Sheriff Pratt could stop being, well, a prat and aim at someone who could actually be shot effectively.</p>\n<p>Who’s left?  Iron Legacy?  Ugh.  Well, there’s a lot of damage potential (Bunker, Setback, Dark Watch Mister Fixer, Tachyon if she can bury enough cards) and ongoing-destruction potential (Tachyon, Argent Adept, Setback) in that remaining five-person group, though probably it’s just suicide, but who knows, maybe I’ll give it a shot tomorrow.</p>",
        "post_number": 273,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:32:34.277Z",
