      {
        "id": 103445,
        "name": "Rabk",
        "username": "Rabk",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabk/{size}/1978_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-07-11T04:40:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Finished off Miss Information on advanced mode with NM, Papa legs, Redeemer Fanatic, and Unity in Atlantis. It was a long slow slog, but they got it done.</p><p>The real story was in their first failed attempt, however. Ms. Twain opened with a Diversionary Tactics, chaining into another Diversionary Tactics, and then a Missing Resources. At the end of the first villain turn the heroes were running in circles trying to deal with a \"Cat\" Stuck in a Tree, an \"Old Lady\" in the Street, a \"Diplomatic\" Envoy, and a \"Threat\" to the President. Oh, and every one-shot in their opening hands had been discarded. They chased the \"Cat\" into a Phosphorescent Chamber and got so confused by all the shiny lights that they dropped even more of their stuff on the ground. They began to get a clue about their demure seceratary shortly thereafter, however, when they began to hurt even worse than before. \"Oh,\" said Miss Information, \"What Doesn't Kill You just makes you... &lt;<span>snigger</span>&gt;&nbsp;<em>stronger</em>&nbsp;&lt;snicker&gt;.\"</p><p>So at the end of the second villain turn (remember that&nbsp;<span>that each hero had already discarded 2-3 cards at this point)</span><span>:</span></p><ol>\n<li><span>Destroy 3 hero ongoing or equipment cards.</span></li>\n<li>The player with the most cards in play must destroy 1 of their non-character cards.</li>\n<li>Deal the 2 hero targets with the highest HP 6 melee damage each.</li>\n<li>Deal the 2 hero targets with the highest HP 5 melee damage and 5 energy damage each.</li>\n<li>Deal the 2 hero targets with the lowest HP 5 cold damage each.</li>\n</ol><p><span>Yeah, they don't really like to talk about \"that one time in Atlantis.\" Tempest will never let them live that one down.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 274,
